 Every task has an `id`, a unique string that stays the same when the task is renamed. `list.get(id)` returns
 the task with that id. `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept either a
 title or an id; an id wins if it is also some task's title.
+
+## Timestamps
+
+Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings. They are equal when the task is
+added; every change (`complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`) sets `updatedAt` to the time of the
+change. A change that alters nothing (tagging with a tag the task has, renaming to its own title) or is
+refused leaves `updatedAt` as it was. `createTodoList` takes an optional clock, `() => Date`, for tests.
