+---
+id: task-002-record-task-createdat-and-updatedat
+type: task
+title: "Record task createdAt and updatedAt"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings. When a task is added the two are
+equal. Every change (complete, reopen, rename, tag, untag) sets `updatedAt` to the time of the change.
+
+## Done
+
+`Task` gains `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. The domain does not read the clock (rule r3): `createTaskList`
+takes a clock, and `createTodoList` in `src/index.ts` defaults it to the system time. A change that alters
+nothing (tagging with a tag already present, untagging an absent one, renaming to the same title) leaves
+`updatedAt` as it was; a refused change leaves the task untouched. Tests in `test/list.test.ts`;
+documented in `README.md`.
